WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-Our next guest represents

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
Massachusetts'
7th Congressional District

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Congresswoman Ayanna Pressley.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for bein' here!

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, Seth!

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.642 line:92%
It's great to be with you.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are spending quarantine
with your husband;

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
your stepdaughter;

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have a cat,
a cat of note.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:21.688
-Yes. Her name is
Sojourner Truth Pressley Harris.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We call her Sojo.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's got a mean
resting feline face

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.028 line:92%
and, you know, we love her

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She's great.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.730 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-She's a large cat, yes?

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.731 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Okay, now, watch it.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a body-positive
household, okay?

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-I know that I showed her

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.504
to some of your producers
and there was a little bit

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a reaction.
She is fluffy.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay gotcha.
-She's got no problems.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
Body-positive, okay?
-Alright.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Understood, understood.
-Alright.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-She is exactly the cat

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.447 size:81% position:41% line:92%
she is supposed to be.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly! Exactly.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
We love her.
-One of the things

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
the squad is addressing,
the progressive wing

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.222
of the party is addressing -
I think, you know, in general,

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
everyone in the country should
be addressing right now --

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.859 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is the racial disparity

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how this pandemic
is affecting this country

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that the inequality
that was baked in before thi

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.636 line:92%
is what is leading to that

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you, one,
address it now, in the moment,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.241
in the middle of a crisis,
while, at the same time,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to address
the root causes of it,

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make sure
it doesn't happen again?

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, the thing is
the inequities

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.284 size:88% position:44%
and racial disparities
that we see playing out,

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:27.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
spotlighted and exacerbate
during COVID-19,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.557 size:84% position:42%
have been systemically
entrenched and embedded

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.925 size:78% position:39% line:92%
for a very long time.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.960 line:92%
So, anecdotally, we already knew

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.929 size:81% position:41%
how this would trend
and how this would go.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:39.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, early on, myself
and several of my colleagues

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.567 size:81% position:41% line:92%
began banging the drum

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the collection
of racial data in real time,

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.339
the disaggregation of it,
the public reporting of it

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.975
so that we can ensure that
our public health response

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
is equitable, both in testin
and access to treatment.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.415
You know, here's the thing
is we started out behind.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.518
We are in the worst position
ever, that you wanna be in

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.986 line:92%
in confronting a pandemic,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.590
and that has everything to d
with the criminal negligence

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
the science denials,
press briefings

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.795
that have really functioned more
like disinformation campaigns,

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.831
and the sluggish response
of this administration.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.432 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So we're behind.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so data,
and, particularly, racial data

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
is one way that we get
ahead of that,

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:19.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we ensure the resources
follow the data

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:23.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they are directed
to highest infection rates

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.544 line:92%
most vulnerable communities,

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we can do mobile testing,
antibody testing,

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
contact tracing,
and all of those things

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are in the best interes
of the public health.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, after that,
you know, I think

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.256
it's why we have to suppor
our community health centers

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to address
health disparities --

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
the comorbidities
of structural racism,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
the impact
of climate injustices,

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of food injustices.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is why Black
and Latinx communities,

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.604 size:84% position:42%
which are food deserts;
transportation deserts;

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
higher rates of asthma,
because they disproportionatel

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
bear the burden
of environmental injustices;

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.745 line:92%
have been more susceptible

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.713 line:92%
COVID-19 doesn't discriminate.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.049 size:75% position:38%
You know, anyone can
contract the virus.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
But these communities --
my community --

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
is most susceptible
to contracting it

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:12.025
and, when we do, suffering
the most severe consequences

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.394
-You've talked about this
as a crisis within a crisi

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, obviously, you know,
Congress is having to addres

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
so much that is going
wrong right now.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.135 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you feel as though

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Democratic leadership
is being helpful addressin

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of this angle of the
situation we're in right now

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know, myself,
community members, activists

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.215
and my colleagues, we're focused
on putting the people first.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not corporations,
not private,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.786 line:92%
not profit, not corporations

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:43.556
and focused on the acknowledging
that this is unprecedented hurt.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.757 line:92%
This is a tsunami of hurt.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And experts recently said
that, you know,

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe 90% of these
infections and fatalities

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.766 size:81% position:41%
could've been stopped,
had we acted sooner.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.970
And so what I'll be focused on
in upcoming relief packages is

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.739
"What do we do in the mids
of this unprecedented hurt

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
that provides
the most relief for people?"

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's about getting cas
in the pockets of people

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.380 size:84% position:42% line:92%
as quickly as possible.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.982 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's about more testing.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about canceling
student debt,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.721 line:92%
canceling rent and mortgages.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.924 size:84% position:42%
It's about including
our immigrant neighbors

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.094
who have been excluded today
from every relief package.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about supports
for our most vulnerable --

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
those experiencing homelessnes
and living in shelter,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also incarcerated
men and women.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, beyond that,
I just want to say this --

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fact that we needed
a moment like this

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
to prove to us
who are essential workers.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.443 line:92%
They've always been essentia

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they should've
never been treated

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.146 line:92%
as if they are disposable,

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's how
we've been functioning.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
They should be working
at a living wage.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
We could've already
addressed that.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.186 line:92%
We must do that in the future.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
Having hazard pay,
paid sick leave,

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.324 line:92%
paid family and medical leave.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.793
So the path forward is tha
we've gotta move boldly.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
When people say they can't
wait to be returned to normal,

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
normal, Seth,
was unjust, insufficient,

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.900 line:92%
and inadequate, to begin with,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
so this is an opportunity,
both in addressing

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:06.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
the racial disparities
and in centering the humanit

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the dignity
of every individual,

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
of every family,
of every worker.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.344 line:92%
Then, we've gotta go bold.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
Think about how we
would've weathered this

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we already had
universal healthcare,

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
if people were already working
at a living wage,

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we already had
universal paid sick leave

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.220 line:92%
and paid family medical leave.

